# Version follows semver. 1.0.0 was tagged on 2026-11-10 (docs/release_checklist.md); the
# software DOI is added once Zenodo mints it for the release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "neptune-fork: rebuilding Le Verrier's 1846 Neptune prediction as a Bayesian inference"
# The abstract is .zenodo.json's description, plus the data dedication.
abstract: >-
  neptune-fork rebuilds Le Verrier's 1846 prediction of Neptune from Uranus's observed motion,
  from first principles: its own Wisdom–Holman symplectic N-body integrator (validated against
  REBOUND), a forward model that fits Uranus's orbit jointly with an unseen perturber, and
  partitioned nested sampling (dynesty) for multimodal posteriors and Bayesian evidence,
  checked by coverage tests on synthetic data. It fits the 279 observations of Le Verrier's own
  1846 Table 77 with an apparent-place observation model and per-observer error calibration.
  The pre-registered fit puts the unseen planet at 325.8° on the night Galle found Neptune,
  with a 68 % interval of 323.6°–327.8°, against Neptune's true 325.87°. The transcribed
  Table 77 is published as a separate dataset (concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24044791). The code
  is MIT; the data in data/historical/ are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.
authors:
  - family-names: Pahadiya
    given-names: Atishay
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1264-1662"
    affiliation: "San José State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/atishaypahadiya/neptune-fork"
# MIT for the code; CC0 1.0 for everything in data/historical/ (see LICENSE; also stated in
